companions.tests:
tests/test_dedup.py has 14 unittest tests on a fake Sims tree under E:\speedkit_test\dedup\tmpXXXX.

The fake tree holds synthetic packages with overlapping identical and conflicting keys:
- identical content stored as zlib vs uncompressed, and RefPack vs uncompressed;
- a corrupt zlib copy (undecidable);
- a package holding one key twice;
- an active-root copy in Mods;
- a protected companion package next to a fake .ts4script, which has a stale copy inside a fake S4S merge;
- a fully redundant merge.

It also holds copies of small real packages: pirumxsim_slider02_neck_Fixed (an S4S merge with manifest and NameMap, copied twice) and KW_LuckyBrats_anims (RefPack and NameMap), plus a package built bit-exact from real slider resources.

What the tests cover:
- HashingTests:
  - status of every key and the two-pass behaviour;
  - a second run reads 0 bytes (cache);
  - the cache survives a Mods/Mods_parked move;
  - effective_map in both scopes;
  - a changed file is not read.
- DedupTests:
  - plan decisions: rewrite, quarantine, skip, protected, active root, NameMap and ignore_namemap;
  - report content, including stale script copies;
  - apply, verify and undo end to end: dry run changes nothing; default journal home stays inside the fake tree; m1 loses exactly the dropped keys and its manifest no longer lists them; the real slider's manifest is rewritten; no temp files remain; undo restores every file bit for bit;
  - winner policy;
  - a forced invariant violation is undone automatically;
  - a stale plan is refused;
  - the free-space guard;
  - the free-space model for a quarantine on the same drive and on another drive;
  - the game started mid-run: stops after 1 package, the undo is refused while the game runs, and a later undo restores everything;
  - two index entries at the same offset give a skip.

Run: python -m unittest discover -s tests -p "test_dedup*.py" -v
Result: "Ran 14 tests in 7.648s" / "OK". No temp folders are left behind.

Read-only checks on the real library:
- For all three policies, a simulation of each plan's end state from the hashes gave no changed and no missing key, in both the Mods+Mods_parked and the Mods-only scope.
- No protected package is in any plan.
- Afterwards, nothing new existed under the Sims 4 folder (no SpeedKit folder, no temp files).
